## ⏰ 3. Maintenance & Automated Backups (Systemd Timers)

* Use native systemd timers instead of legacy cron jobs for better logging via `journalctl`:
  ```ini
  # /etc/systemd/system/nas-backup.timer
  [Unit]
  Description=Run daily NAS backup

  [Timer]
  OnCalendar=*-*-* 03:00:00
  Persistent=true

  [Install]
  WantedBy=timers.target
  ```
* **Drive Mount Protection:** In `/etc/fstab`, always include `nofail,x-systemd.device-timeout=10s` for external USB storage so the server boots normally even if a drive is disconnected.
